[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: November 3 Overnight Rust Survivor Regression Contracts

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SURV-20261103-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Artifact identifier byte boundary
STATEMENT: >>>
Publication shall accept valid ASCII identifiers of 1 through 128 bytes inclusive and reject longer, empty or invalid-alphabet identifiers before creating storage.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: src/artifact.rs::publish. Verification: tests/overnight_survivors_20261103.rs::run_id_boundary_and_invalid_alphabet_preserve_storage; evidence/rust-survivors-20261103.md. The trusted-root filesystem contract is unchanged.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: REF-006

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SURV-20261103-002
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Differential switch control audit
STATEMENT: >>>
The DC physical audit shall reconstruct switch control as CP minus CN, preserving the accepted midpoint current under a common-mode control shift and detecting an incorrect returned output state.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: src/audit.rs::dc_currents. Verification: tests/overnight_survivors_20261103.rs differential-switch and midpoint common-mode property cases. Expected midpoint resistance is independently derived as the geometric mean of endpoint resistances. This checks control wiring and conservation; the existing model law remains shared and is not a wholly independent switch-model implementation.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: REF-006

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SURV-20261103-003
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Direct DC audit Gmin boundary
STATEMENT: >>>
The direct DC audit shall admit finite positive fixed Gmin through one siemens inclusive and reject larger, nonpositive or nonfinite values; retained shunts shall participate in current and power balance.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: src/audit.rs::dc. Verification: tests/overnight_survivors_20261103.rs::direct_gmin_audit_includes_one_siemens_and_rejects_larger_or_nonfinite. Analytical reference: a 2 A supply at 2 V balances the 1 S shunt. No numerical solver participates in this test.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: REF-006
